# Copy to .riskscanignore at your repo root. Entries are matched most-specific-first:
#
#   <file>:<rule>:<line>    this one finding
#   <file>:<rule>           that rule anywhere in that file
#   <rule>                  that rule everywhere
#
# The trailing comment is the reason. It is shown every time the finding is suppressed, because
# a suppressed finding is still reported as a counted white line — never silently dropped.
#
# Rule ids are slugs of the rule label (`AWS access key id` -> `aws-access-key-id`) for the
# builtin pack, and gitleaks' own RuleIDs for gitleaks findings. When a finding blocks a commit
# the hook prints the exact entry to paste.
#
# A personal, uncommitted allowlist can live at ~/.riskscan/ignore instead.

docs/cookbook.md:aws-access-key-id:42   # AWS's documented example key, in a doc
terraform/examples:generic-api-key      # vendor sample values
